From: HakiOS
Subject: [PATCH 0167] sweet: bilinear scaled panel copy (sweetfb_filter=1) and copy time stat

The scaled copy of a 750x1624 frame (crop 720x1600) to the 1080x2400 panel is nearest
neighbour: at 1.5x every second source row and column is shown twice, which the user sees as
pixelated. Boot-arg sweetfb_filter=1 makes the scaled copy bilinear: pixel-centre mapping,
2x2 source pixels blended per channel in integer SWAR (no FP, no NEON), each panel pixel
written once and in order, the panel never read; the last source row and column are never
passed (weight 0 there). The band's cache invalidate covers the bottom source row too.
sweetfb_filter=0 (default) keeps the nearest path as it was; the 1:1 path is untouched.
Logged at start: "SWEET FB: scaled copy filter nearest|bilinear".

Also: time in copy() for both paths, once a second when there were copies:
"SWEET FB copy: N copies, avg X us, max Y us".

Not compiled locally; CI is the compiler.
